                <pb facs="0372" n="300" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg300"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 12655/35.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the British
                    Ambassador.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-09-29"><hi rendition="#italic">September 29,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note No. 195, of the 25th instant, with regard to the
                    forthcoming international law conference in London, and to say in reply that the
                    contents of your note will have the department’s consideration.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Bacon.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
